   =========================================================
   Box Shadow
   =========================================================

   box-shadow is used to add shadow effects around elements,
   giving depth and a raised or floating appearance.

   Syntax:
   box-shadow: offset-x offset-y blur-radius spread-radius color;

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   VALUES EXPLANATION
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   offset-x:
   - Horizontal position of the shadow
   - Positive → right
   - Negative → left

   offset-y:
   - Vertical position of the shadow
   - Positive → down
   - Negative → up

   blur-radius:
   - Controls softness of the shadow
   - Larger value → softer shadow

   spread-radius:
   - Controls size of the shadow
   - Positive → expands shadow
   - Negative → shrinks shadow

   color:
   - Shadow color (rgba is commonly used)

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   COMMON EXAMPLES
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Light shadow:
   box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);

   Deep shadow:
   box-shadow: 0 6px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);

   Inner shadow:
   box-shadow: inset 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   EASY RULE TO REMEMBER
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Small blur → sharp shadow
   Large blur → soft shadow
   inset → shadow inside the element
